            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "The relative error shows how the root mean square error between the in situ data and the unbiased ERA-I data compares with the standard deviation of the in situ data. It helps to compare the error to the internal variability of the in situ data.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "ERA-Interim",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "standard deviation",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "We also evaluate how the standard deviation of the ERA-Interim products before and after correction differs from the one of the FLUXNET data set by calculating normalized standard deviations (SD(E)/SD(FE) and SD(Ed)/SD(FE), respectively) in order to evaluate how much the data variability is maintained.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "ERA-Interim",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "correlation",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Lastly, we specifically evaluate the diurnal cycle interpolated from the 3-hourly de-biased meteorological fields of the ERA-I data set. To this end, two new time series have been constructed from F and Ed by removing their daily mean values. The correlation between these two \u201canomaly\u201d time series is calculated at each site, as is the standard deviation of the time series inferred from the ERA-I data set, normalized to the standard deviation of the one inferred from the FLUXNET data set.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "ERA-Interim",
            "source_entity_type": "Source",
            "relation": "HAS_METRIC",
            "target_entity_instance": "normalized standard deviation",
            "target_entity_type": "Metric",
            "paragraph": "Figure 2 represents the normalized standard deviation (NSD) of the ERA-I products (Ta, VPD, WS, Rg and LWin) before and after the bias correction, and, consequently, it gives insights into how the de-biasing procedure impacts the internal variability of the meteorological fields",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
